                <pb facs="0308" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0011/11–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-26T11:00:00-05:00">November 26, 1948—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1705. Personal for Stuart. Please inform Madame Chiang that in accordance with
                    her telephone request to me and her subsequent request through Admiral Badger
                    for transportation to the United States, arrangements have been made for Admiral
                    Badger to furnish air transportation for Madame Chiang and party for temporary
                    visit to the United States.</p>
                <p>Our immigration people have been alerted that entry clearance should be given in
                    the event passports and visas are not in order.</p>
                <p>Advise me immediately of party and itinerary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
